TITLE:: RCBeat
summary:: One pattern voice with a live-editable attribute set
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Guides/reCurrent, Classes/RCLayer, Classes/RCBeatSpec, Classes/RCDurList

DESCRIPTION::
The successor of the proto-library's beat env + PLbindef. The pattern is an link::Classes/RCPbindProxy:: (an link::Classes/RCKeyProxy:: per key) whose pairs are, in order: code::[\rc_beat, beat] ++ addFirst ++ [\dur_unadj, realDur, \dur, pipeline] ++ [\midiout, \chan] ++ attrDict ++ [\rc_finish]::, wrapped in a guarding code::Prout::. A static value is read as it is; every other key has one Routine of its own, seeded per key, instead of the two to four per key of code::PbindProxy::, with the same seeded output.

The dur pipeline computes code::dur = dur_unadj + swing(timeTrack) - previous swing offset::, clamps non-positive values to link::#*minDur:: (zero-length rests pass) and stops the beat after link::#*maxClampedInARow:: clamped events in a row. The last pair clamps negative code::legato:: / code::sustain::.

Errors raised by any key stream are caught: with the default policy code::\restart:: the stream is rebuilt after code::restartDelay:: beats, up to code::maxRestarts:: consecutive failures; with code::\stop:: the beat stops at the first error. Other beats are never affected.

Every non-static value is mirrored: link::#-lastValue:: returns the last value a key produced, link::#-thread:: its Routine and link::#-randData:: its random state (settable, to replay the key).

