SUBSECTION:: Lag monitor

How far behind logical time the interpreter runs when an event is about to play (code::Main.elapsedTime - thisThread.seconds::, measured in the last key). scsynth prints strong::late:: once this exceeds code::server.latency::. Opt-in: it costs one subtraction per event.

code::
RCBeat.lagReset; RCBeat.lagMonitor = true;   // before a section
RCBeat.lagReport;                            // after it: "lag: max 12.3 ms (beat hl3/rhythm_t1/orgnsm_percs_path_t1_4), mean 0.8 ms, 0 of 2304 events over 0.8 of the latency"
::

METHOD:: lagMonitor
When true, every event records its lag (default false).
METHOD:: lagWarnRatio
Above code::lagWarnRatio * server.latency:: a rate-limited warning names the beat (default 0.8).
METHOD:: lagReset
Clear the counters.
METHOD:: lagReport
One line: the worst event and its beat, the mean, how many events crossed the ratio.
METHOD:: lagMax
METHOD:: lagMaxTag
METHOD:: lagCount
METHOD:: lagLateCount
METHOD:: lagByTag
code::IdentityDictionary:: beat tag → worst lag in seconds.

